# Chapter 5, part 3: the markers from Filedate to Keycap, without those that
# are printed as a label (they are in markers5).

.h2 Filedate [marker-filedate]
.ix Filedate marker
.ix Marker, Filedate
.ix Date of the file
The Filedate marker prints the date on which the document was last saved, that
is, the modification date of its file on disk.  Use it for "last changed on".
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | Format.
Global setting | Date Format on the Marker Format panel of Global, Marker.
.end
.h3 The panel
.table 11 15 9 22
Field | Values | Default | Effect
Format | The date words of the Date marker ({n:marker-date}) | Month D, Year (or
  |  | the Date Format of the document) | How the date is written.
.end
.h3 On the screen
The label is the word FILEDATE in Short and Long and FDATE in Name; the date of
the file is made when the document is printed.
.h3 When printed
The date and nothing else, as text.  The date is that of the file as it is on
disk when the Printer works: the changes that have not been saved are not in
it.
.h3 Edges
- A document that has no file (a new document, or one that was never saved)
  has no date of a file, and the date of the day is printed.
- A print of a part of the document (a block, a range of sections) has the
  date of the same file.

.h2 Filename [marker-filename]
.ix Filename marker
.ix Marker, Filename
The Filename marker prints the name of the document file, without its
directory.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | None.  The marker is inserted at once.
.end
.h3 On the screen
Short and Long: the name, in capital letters, in brackets, such as
[PROPOSAL.DOC] (a document that has no name yet shows [FILENAME]).  Name:
[FNAME].
.h3 When printed
The name of the file, in capital letters, with the extension, for example
PROPOSAL.DOC.  A document with no name prints FILENAME.  The Printer prints the
name according to the display mode of the marker
({n:markers-print-modes}).  The name is that of your document, also when only
a part of it is printed (a block, a range of sections) and in Preview.
.h3 Edges
The capital letters are made by the program whatever the case of the file name
on disk.  Use the Pathname marker ({n:marker-pathname}) when the directory is
needed too.

.h2 Filetime [marker-filetime]
.ix Filetime marker
.ix Marker, Filetime
The Filetime marker prints the time of day at which the document was last
saved, the modification time of its file.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | Format.
Global setting | Time Format on the Marker Format panel of Global, Marker.
.end
.h3 The panel
.table 11 15 9 22
Field | Values | Default | Effect
Format | The time words of the Time marker ({n:marker-time}) | H:MM am/pm (or
  |  | the Time Format of the document) | How the time is written.
.end
.h3 On the screen
FILETIME in Short and Long, FTIME in Name.
.h3 When printed
The time of the file as text.
.h3 Edges
- As with the Filedate marker ({n:marker-filedate}), a document without a file
  prints the time now.

.h2 Font [marker-font]
.ix Font marker
.ix Marker, Font
.ix Change of typeface
.ix Typeface list
A Font marker changes the family of type of the text that follows it, to the
end of the block.  Put it before the words that are to be in another typeface,
and put a second Font marker, with the choice [Text], to go back.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | Font.
Global setting | The Typeface panel of Global names the twenty fonts
 ({n:format-marker}).
.end
.h3 The panel
.table 11 15 9 22
Field | Values | Default | Effect
Font | [Text: name], Headline: name, Text: name, Header/Footer: name,
  | Font 4: name to Font 20: name | [Text] | The font of the text after
 the marker.
.end
.pic pictures/markers-font.png 5.4 The list of the Font marker: the font of the block first, then the fonts 1 to 20.
Each entry shows the role or number of the font and the name that the Typeface
panel gives it, for example Font 7: Palatino; a font that has no name shows
"not set".  The first entry, in brackets, is the font that the block has; the
other entries are the fonts 1 to 20.  {k:Keypad +}, {k:Alt-+} and {k:F2} show
the list.
.h3 On the screen
The default mode is Short, which shows [FONT].  In the Long mode the label is
the word Font; in Name mode it is FONT; Diamond shows a diamond.  The screen has one typeface, so the text is not drawn
differently.
.h3 When printed
The Printer uses the name of the font only to choose one of three families of
type: the typewriter family if the name holds one of the words program, code,
courier, mono, typewriter, fixed, listing or source; the sans serif family if
it holds head, title, sans, helv, arial or gothic (but Header/Footer is not a
headline name); and the roman family for any other name.  The family stays in
force to the end of the block.  The size, the style and the real typeface of
the name are not used.  A Font marker with the choice [Text] returns to the
family of the block.  A font that has no name is the roman family.
The sample {c:fonts-sample.doc} in the directory
{c:share/strata/samples/fonts} shows the fonts of the Typeface list, the
numbers 1 to 20, one section for each font.  The headline of a section reads
Font 4: Times: the Section Tag of the first level makes the number, which is
the number of the font ({n:format-set-tags}).  A font that has nothing
configured, the number 20, has the line nothing configured. and no sizes;
each of the other fonts is shown at five sizes.  Lato, the number 19, is
printed in its own typeface only after it is installed ({n:str-fonts-install});
until then the Printer sets its sizes in the font of the text.  The sample
sets the font and the size with a LaTeX marker, because a Font marker cannot
set a size.
.h3 Edges
The marker applies to the end of the block, not to the end of the line.

.h2 Keep [marker-keep]
.ix Keep marker
.ix Marker, Keep
.ix Keep blocks on one page
.ix Start (Fixed), Start (Floating), End
A Keep marker keeps blocks together on a page: the blocks from a Start marker to
the End marker are printed on one page, so that a table, a program listing or a
figure and its caption are not split.  A Keep marker is never printed; it only
changes where the pages break.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | Keep.
.end
.h3 The panel
.table 11 15 9 22
Field | Values | Default | Effect
Keep | Start (Fixed), Start (Floating), End | Start (Fixed) | What the marker
 is.
.end
.table 13 47
Choice | What it does
Start (Fixed) | Begins a region.  If the region does not fit on the rest of the
 page, it moves to the next page whole, and the rest of this page stays empty;
 the text that follows the region stays after it.
Start (Floating) | Begins a region.  If the region does not fit, it moves to
 the next page and the blocks that follow the End fill the rest of this page,
 in front of it.
End | Ends the region that the last Start began.
.end
.h3 How the regions are made
The unit of a region is the whole block, or the whole table when a marker is in
one of its rows.  The rules are these.
- A Start inside a region is ignored: the first End closes the region.  Pairs
  do not nest.
- An End with no Start before it is ignored.
- A Start with no End keeps the text from the Start to the end of the document.
- A region is broken at the start of a section: the part of a region that
  lies in each section is kept on its own, and a headline stays with the first
  kept block after it.
- A block that holds Keep markers and nothing else takes no height.
- A region that is longer than a page cannot be kept: it starts at the top of
  a new page and goes on over the next ones as usual.
- A region that holds a Page Break, a Column Break or an Orientation marker is
  not kept, and neither is a region that begins in the text of the title page of
  a structured document (the text before the first section).  The Keep markers
  are dropped and the text is set as if they were not there.
- A footnote in a kept region is printed at the foot of the page where the
  region is placed.
.h3 On the screen
The default is Long: Start Keep (Fixed), Start Keep (Floating) or End Keep in
brackets.  Short is the same.  Name: [KEEP].
.h3 When printed
Nothing is printed for the marker, in a Final print, in a Draft print and in a
Preview.  The blocks of the region are put on one page: a Fixed region that
does not fit in the rest of the page starts on the next page, and a Floating
region that does not fit moves to the next page while the text that follows
fills the rest of this one.  A Floating region that is taller than nine tenths
of the page is placed like a Fixed one.
.h3 Edges
- The marker is better placed in a block of its own, before the first block and
  after the last block of the region.  A Start in the middle of a block
  keeps that whole block.
- A table kept in a region is set row by row without a break inside a row; the
  rows are the unit.
- The Keep marker is a different feature from the Keep Block on One Page
  field of the local formats, which is in {n:format}.

.h2 Keycap [marker-keycap]
.ix Keycap marker
.ix Marker, Keycap
.ix Key legends
.ix Keycaps
A Keycap marker draws a key, a small rounded box with a legend in it, in the
line of text.  The manual itself uses it for every key name.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | Legend, Foreground, Background, Scale, Font.
Global setting | Keycap Format of Global, Marker, which gives the values that a
 marker without a value of its own takes ({n:format-marker-ring}).
.end
.h3 The panel
.table 11 15 9 22
Field | Values | Default | Effect
Legend | Text, such as Enter, {k:F12} or {k:Ctrl-S} | None (required) | The text in the
 key.
Foreground | 0.0 to 100.0 | [0.0] (the Keycap Format) | The shade of the legend
 and of the line of the key; 0.0 is black.
Background | 0.0 to 100.0 | [100.0] | The shade of the fill of the key; 100.0 is
 white.
Scale | 0.001 to 10 | [1.000] | The size of the whole key, as a multiple
 of the size of the text around it.
Font | [Text: name], then the twenty fonts | [Text] | The font of the legend;
 only the family is used.
.end
.pic pictures/markers-keycap.png 5.4 The panel of the Keycap marker, with the legend Ctrl-S.
The defaults are shown in brackets: the value of the Keycap Format of the
document.  A value that is typed replaces the bracket and stays in the
marker, also when it equals the global one.  A field that is left at the
bracket follows the Keycap Format.
.h3 On the screen
The default mode is Inline.  In the X11 version a key is drawn as a picture of
the rounded box, in the colors of the editor (a Foreground of 0.0 is the color
of the text and a Background of 100.0 the color of the window).  In the
terminal version, and while the picture is not ready, the key is the legend in
reverse video with a space on each side.  When the picture cannot be made
(LaTeX is not installed, LaTeX finds a mistake, or the job takes more than five
seconds) the key is shown as [Key: legend], its Short form, never as an
empty box.  The cursor on it brings the message "Keycap drawn as Short: ..."
with the cause, and the log of the run ({n:appcfg-log}) has one entry with the
block and the line.  The other modes show [Key: legend] (Short and Long), [KEY]
(Name), a diamond or nothing.
.h3 When printed
A key is printed as a box with rounded corners and a thin line, as high as
the line of text and wide enough for the legend, with the legend in the family
of the font (roman if the font has no name that says otherwise).  The
Foreground sets the shade of the legend and of the line, the Background the
fill, and the Scale the size.  The shades are between 0.0 and 100.0 and the
scale between 0.001 and 10: a value out of range is rejected with a message
({n:markers-messages}).
.h3 Edges
- The legend is plain text; it is printed as it is typed.
- The size of the font is ignored: the size of the key comes from the scale and
  the text around it.
- A key is a word: it is in the line and is moved with it.
- An empty Legend gives No string specified.
